WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.915 --> 00:00:04.160
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm&nbsp;
Jan and today we're taking a deep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.880
dive into the ending of Season 5 Part 1 to&nbsp;
explain the daddy of all get-togethers,
&nbsp;

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.920
what the hell Michael is really up to, whether a&nbsp;
demon can actually get a soul, plus predictions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.240
and theories for Part 2 and Season 6!
Just before we begin, many thanks to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.560
sponsor of this video, Raid Shadow Legends.
We will, of course, be talking spoilers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.280
so take care if you're not all caught up.
Michael's elaborate plan to ruin his brother's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:32.240
life appears to be working by the end of Part 1.
He's not only turned Maze against Lucifer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:37.200
but he's triggered Amenadiel's fears to&nbsp;
spiral out of control causing time to freeze.
&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.480
And as the battle between Team Lucifer and Team&nbsp;
Michael comes to a head, in the very final moments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:48.640
of the Part 1 finale, God arrives to intervene.
"That's enough! Children.
&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.680
You know I hate it when you fight."
Lucifans have been wondering when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:55.840
God would finally turn up on the show,
and given the first episode of the second part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:01.200
Season 5 is called "Family Dinner", we can expect&nbsp;
to see some interesting family dynamics between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.440
God, Lucifer, Michael, and Amenadiel.
And perhaps Luci's other siblings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:11.120
Remy and Azrael, will also make an appearance.
Lucifer's family reunion in the next episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.520
is bound to relate back to the moment&nbsp;
in Season 5's first episode when Luci&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.920
takes Lee to his parents' house where they&nbsp;
were celebrating his sister's baby shower.
&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.840
Lee says he can't go in to see them because&nbsp;
he's ashamed of what they think of him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.240
and Lucifer proceeds to berate him:
"Sooner or later, you are going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:33.840
disappoint them all over again! 
And so you'd rather stay away for all eternity."
&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:39.280
As Lee points out, and Lucifer soon realises,&nbsp;
this situation isn't just about Lee;
&nbsp;

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:43.520
in fact, it reveals Luci's feelings&nbsp;
about how he relates to his own family.
&nbsp;

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.720
"This isn't just about me, is it?
Whose Hell is this anyway?"
&nbsp;

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:51.200
With Lucifer's dad arriving on the scene,&nbsp;
Lucifer will finally have to confront his own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.920
feelings of shame towards his celestial family.
It'll be interesting to see if Luci continues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.680
to feel guilty for his rebellion&nbsp;
or if he can re-join his family.
&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.640
Although Lucifer previously said in Season 4 that&nbsp;
he was lying to himself about God manipulating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:09.920
everything in his life, faced with his Father&nbsp;
now, will any of those old feelings resurface?
&nbsp;

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.680
"If you mean his plan to continually&nbsp;
manipulate and control me, then agreed."
&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:17.280
Also, will Lucifer confront God&nbsp;
over his Mother's claims that God&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.560
wanted to destroy Luci after the rebellion?
"I asked him to send you to Hell instead."
&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.920
And if the Goddess was manipulating&nbsp;
Lucifer about that, it'll be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:30.720
intriguing to hear God's version of events.
After all, in the "alternate universe" bonus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.320
episode, God said that "a parent just&nbsp;
wants what's best for their child".
&nbsp;

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.000
But, of course, Michael will&nbsp;
be at the family reunion too
&nbsp;

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.080
and we know from Amenadiel that Michael has&nbsp;
positioned himself as God's only trusted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.920
advisor to the point that no other&nbsp;
being in Heaven can speak to God. 
&nbsp;

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.960
"He is stronger than you think, Lucy.
Michael's become...
&nbsp;

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.320
untouchable in the Silver City."
So, what is Michael's grand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:56.480
plan and what's he really up to?
Well, when Michael explained to Maze why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.960
he came to Earth, he said that he was annoyed at&nbsp;
the praise Lucifer was getting from all the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.760
angels after he returned to Hell voluntarily.
"Then Raphael starts going off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.120
about how Lucifer's grown,
and then pretty soon all I hear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.760
is, 'Lucifer, Lucifer, Lucifer!'"
Michael's jealous that Luci is getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:18.240
kudos for doing what he views as the bare&nbsp;
minimum, just fulfilling his basic role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:22.320
something he'd previously been shirking.
Michael also appears to be threatened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.200
by his twin brother's growing maturity and&nbsp;
ability to sacrifice his own happiness in LA&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.280
in order to save those he cares for&nbsp;
and do his duty as ruler of Hell.
&nbsp;

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.800
If God believes that Lucifer has&nbsp;
redeemed himself for his rebellion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.600
then Michael's favoured position in Heaven&nbsp;
sitting at God's right hand may be in danger.
&nbsp;

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.040
Because of his inferiority&nbsp;
complex in relation to his twin,
&nbsp;

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:47.040
Michael has been constantly plotting to have&nbsp;
Lucifer make decisions that will make him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:52.320
look "unworthy" in God's eyes all the while&nbsp;
raising his own status in the Silver City.
&nbsp;

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.040
As Amenadiel pointed out:
"You're terrified that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:59.040
Lucifer is better than you.
That he'll always be better than you."
&nbsp;

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.520
According to Michael, he claims he's been&nbsp;
secretly planting ideas in Lucifer's mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.760
from starting an uprising against God&nbsp;
to his antics in the Garden of Eden.
&nbsp;

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.920
Michael even says he was responsible&nbsp;
for giving Luci the idea to abandon his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:17.440
responsibilities in Hell to come to Los Angeles.
Of course, given Michael's tendency to tell lies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.600
it's possible his claims of controlling&nbsp;
Lucifer's actions are actually false,
&nbsp;

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:25.280
and that what he's really doing by telling&nbsp;
his brother that he's been playing him all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:29.040
this time is preying on Luci's fears;
because if there's one thing we know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.960
about Lucifer, it's that he does not like&nbsp;
to feel that he's being manipulated. 
&nbsp;

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.200
Another part of Michael's plan has&nbsp;
been to exploit Chloe's fears around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.720
her relationship with Lucifer.
After Michael abducts Chloe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:45.680
he exposes her concern that Lucifer hasn't&nbsp;
said the exact words "I love you" to her,
&nbsp;

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.760
something that begins to prey on her mind,
&nbsp;

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:52.400
in particular given that earlier Ella was&nbsp;
raving about Pete's "I love meatloaf" line.
&nbsp;

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.320
"How long did it take Lucifer&nbsp;
to say 'I love you'?"
&nbsp;

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:59.520
Michael also tries to worry Chloe about Lucifer's&nbsp;
new-found invincibility when he's with her.
&nbsp;

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.720
"Him choosing to be vulnerable&nbsp;
around you actually meant something.
&nbsp;

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:05.600
Cause you do know that we angels,&nbsp;
we self-actualize, right?"
&nbsp;

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:10.720
So, when Chloe's reunited with Lucifer, she&nbsp;
wonders whether subconsciously he's pushing her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:16.240
away, and if his new invulnerability around her&nbsp;
means he's choosing not be vulnerable with her.
&nbsp;

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:20.800
Now, Michael has obviously amplified Chloe's&nbsp;
fear, but I think it's evident that Lucifer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:24.400
does love her because he finally&nbsp;
attempts to tell her how he feels:
&nbsp;

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.480
"No, Dete-- Chloe.
I...
&nbsp;

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.120
I lo--"
Luci may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:33.840
have been cut off by Amenadiel accidentally&nbsp;
freezing time, but the crucial point to note&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:38.720
here is that Lucifer used Chloe's real name
rather than "Detective", because although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:43.440
he rarely uses her true name, when he does&nbsp;
it signals his true feelings towards her.
&nbsp;

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:46.320
"My first love was never Eve.
It was you, Chloe."
&nbsp;

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:51.120
On top of that, Lucifer was desperate to find&nbsp;
Chloe when she disappeared in the final episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.600
making it clear that he does love her deeply.
&nbsp;

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:58.560
Now, I've got a lot more details to discuss about&nbsp;
Lucifer's new-found invulnerability and the weird&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:03.360
mojo swapping going on between him and Chloe.
That's all in a separate video and I'll add&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:06.960
a card here and a link in the video&nbsp;
description as soon as it's ready.
&nbsp;

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:11.120
When it comes to Maze, she's been&nbsp;
through a rough time so far in Season 5
&nbsp;

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:16.240
leading her to switch allegiance from Team Lucifer&nbsp;
to Team Michael after he promises he'll get her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:19.600
the soul she's been longing for.
At the start of the fifth season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.720
she's already mad at Lucifer for&nbsp;
going down to Hell without her.
&nbsp;

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:27.600
And adding to her abandonment issues are Chloe&nbsp;
who splits up their detective partnership;
&nbsp;

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:32.000
Eve who left her at the end of Season 4;
and then her mother Lilith who dies a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:36.720
days after she sees her again and before&nbsp;
Maze can really tell her how she feels.
&nbsp;

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:41.680
Maze believes her lack of a soul is responsible&nbsp;
for her loneliness and blames Lilith for that:
&nbsp;

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:44.800
"It was her stupid idea to&nbsp;
have soulless offspring...
&nbsp;

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:49.360
making it her stupid fault that I&nbsp;
am doomed to be alone forever."
&nbsp;

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:52.800
And when she asks Lucifer if he's&nbsp;
heard of a demon getting a soul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.440
he enrages her with his dismissive attitude,
even after she points out that nobody heard of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:01.600
the Devil falling in love before, or of an&nbsp;
angel and a human having a baby together.
&nbsp;

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.160
"There's a first for everything, right?"
"Well, that's different.
&nbsp;

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:06.720
We're angels.
You're just a demon."
&nbsp;

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:10.560
The topic of Maze and demons not&nbsp;
having a soul has come up previously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:14.560
in particular in the Maze-focussed&nbsp;
episode "Mr and Mrs Mazikeen Smith":
&nbsp;

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:17.280
"When I die, that's it.
Maze out."
&nbsp;

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:21.120
This season, presenting himself as a&nbsp;
friend to Maze, Michael offers her a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:24.960
soul which is what she thinks she wants;
although, given his tendency for lying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:28.640
and manipulating, that's likely to&nbsp;
turn out to be a ruse of sorts.
&nbsp;

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:33.680
Instead, what I think could be important to&nbsp;
resolving Maze's existential dilemma is Lucifer's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:38.480
ring, which her mother Lilith gave him and&nbsp;
which Maze was staring at in the final episode.
&nbsp;

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:43.200
We learned in the noir episode that Lilith gave&nbsp;
up her immortality when she blew what looked like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:48.560
perhaps her own soul or essence into the ring.
The ring also contains a stone from the Garden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:53.120
of Eden, and so I think it could play a part&nbsp;
in Maze acquiring a soul or something else&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:56.960
that will make her feel complete.
After all, as Amenadiel told her:
&nbsp;

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:00.080
"I don't know if a soul is what&nbsp;
you need to feel whole, but...
&nbsp;

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.720
I do know this.
If anyone is going to find what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:07.520
they're looking for, it's you, Mazikeen."
Perhaps just like Lucifer and Amenadiel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:10.800
we'll learn that Maze has the&nbsp;
ability to self-actualize,
&nbsp;

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.840
and with the help of her mother's&nbsp;
ring, she will come to believe that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:19.200
she isn't just a soulless demon after all.
Like Dorothy with her shoes in the Wizard of Oz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.800
Maze has 'always had the power', she&nbsp;
'just had to learn it for herself'.
&nbsp;

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:27.680
A big reveal at the end of Season 5&nbsp;
is that Amenadiel and Linda's baby boy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:34.000
Charlie appears to be mortal and not half-angel&nbsp;
as everyone had previously assumed in Season 4.
&nbsp;

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:39.040
This could somehow be a trick by Michael,&nbsp;
but Charlie does get frozen in time together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:43.120
with all the other humans in the finale.
And he also got a fever which turned out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:47.600
to be a cold, something that in theory&nbsp;
shouldn't happen to a part-celestial.
&nbsp;

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:52.800
Charlie being an ordinary human does tie in with&nbsp;
a little running gag throughout the fifth season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:57.120
about the baby's parents being over-optimistic&nbsp;
about the extent of his abilities.
&nbsp;

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:02.080
Linda, for example, has arranged everything from&nbsp;
Japanese language classes to art appreciation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:06.000
events for the 2-month old baby, and&nbsp;
she's convinced he can even identify&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:09.760
elements on the Periodic Table.
And Amenadiel tells Dan he thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:14.880
Charlie had some kind of super-strength, but then&nbsp;
discovered he couldn't even hold up his rattle.
&nbsp;

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:19.120
This could all tie back to Lucifer's&nbsp;
theory in Season 4 that explained how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.720
Amenadiel had been able to conceive a&nbsp;
child with Linda in the first place:
&nbsp;

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:26.080
"When you lost your wings, you&nbsp;
became as mortal as it gets.
&nbsp;

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:31.040
Maybe you became more human than you realized."
Perhaps Amenadiel was so human when Charlie was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:35.360
convinced that the baby never inherited&nbsp;
any of his father's celestial powers.
&nbsp;

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:40.640
But there could be something else at play when it&nbsp;
comes to Charlie's human vs celestial nature, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:46.560
it relates to an intriguing incident in Season 3.
In the episode "All About Her", Amenadiel visits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.840
the doctor after getting some&nbsp;
cold and flu-like symptoms.
&nbsp;

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:54.560
Amenadiel says he's never had a human illness,&nbsp;
but then the doctor tells him he has Chlamydia.
&nbsp;

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:57.760
Later on, he discovers, the&nbsp;
diagnosis was a false positive.
&nbsp;

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:01.600
The reason for the test results coming&nbsp;
back wrong was never really explained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:06.320
but it seems reasonable to think it's something&nbsp;
to with him being an angel and not human.
&nbsp;

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:10.160
And I think something very similar happened to&nbsp;
Charlie when he ran a fever which the doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:14.160
diagnosed as a normal human cold.
Something about his half-angel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:18.560
half-human nature is likely at the root of&nbsp;
it, and I expect we'll get an explanation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:22.960
in the second half of Season 5.
Now, there are another eight episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:28.000
still to come in the second part of Season 5 and&nbsp;
there's a sixth and final season after that,
&nbsp;

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:32.160
and I'll be going in depth with more&nbsp;
theories for those in an upcoming video.
&nbsp;

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:37.440
Season 5 was originally expected to be the end of&nbsp;
the show, which means that the sixteenth episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:41.680
would have wrapped up all of the series'&nbsp;
character arcs in a montage of sorts.
&nbsp;

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:44.800
What's going to happen instead&nbsp;
now is that the sixth season will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:49.600
dive deeper into each character's ending.
According to Aimee Garcia, who plays Ella,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:53.440
we may be getting a full episode for&nbsp;
each character in the final season to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:57.760
see in detail where each of them ends up.
The ending then will still be the same as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:02.560
the original ending for Season 5, but it&nbsp;
will just be extended over a full season.
&nbsp;

